                <pb facs="0224" n="104" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg104"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/3417</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                            Lee, Higginson &amp; Company</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-16">June 16, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sirs</hi>: The Department has received your letter of
                    June 9 regarding Dominican financing. The Department is giving the matter
                    careful consideration and, in this connection, would like to be advised more
                    fully what you have in mind regarding a refunding loan mentioned in paragraph
                    (7) on page 7 of your letter under acknowledgement.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis
                            White</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Assistant
                    Secretary</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
